    {
      "id": "5E5000000000000B",
      "title": "Electric Geological Drill",
      "icon": {
        "id": "revoextraction:electric_drill",
        "count": 1
      },
      "x": 6.0,
      "y": 6.0,
      "shape": "circle",
      "dependencies": [
        "5E5000000000000A"
      ],
      "description": [
        "The LV Electric Drill uses 16 EU/t for 200 powered ticks per resource. Mixed cycles silver, nickel, lead, bauxite and antimony; select individual deposits in its menu. Mechanical steel extraction supplies the first battery minerals.",
        "Build it from steel plates, motor, circuits, basic hull and a diamond pickaxe. No exclusive electric-drill metal is required. Hopper insert from the top for upgrades/water; extract resources from other faces.",
        "The Electric Geological Drill is now a 3x3x3 multiblock. Assemble 11 Steel Drill Supports, 8 Steel Drill Casings, 1 Steel Drill Core and this controller. Keep the bottom-centre cell empty. All five native MI hatches belong in the top layer to clear the rotating bit.",
        "Viewed from the front, top layer: back row = Water Input, Sediment Output, Support; middle row = Energy Input, Casing, Item Output; front row = Support, Item Input, Support. Use native steel fluid/item hatches and LV or better energy input. The sediment outlet must face backwards.",
        "Supply 100 mB fresh cooling water per geological cycle. LV programs produce Good Sediment Water; MV/HV geological programs produce Excellent Sediment Water. Drain before changing grade. Full fluid or item outputs stop work without wasting power or coolant. Retained survey cores still gate rare resources."
      ],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "5E5000000010000B",
          "type": "item",
